==============================================================================
PART 1 -- symbolic asymptotic series of c(z) := (1-eps*z)*R(z)/eps as z->inf
==============================================================================
Deriving R(z) asymptotic series via the ODE R'=zR-1 recursion directly
(coefficient recursion, not a canned series-expansion call):
Recursion c_n = -(2n-1) c_{n-1}, c_0=1 gives c_n = [1, -1, 3, -15, 105, -945, 10395, -135135, 2027025]
R(z) ~ 1/z - 1/z**3 + 3/z**5 - 15/z**7 + 105/z**9 - 945/z**11 + 10395/z**13 - 135135/z**15 + 2027025/z**17
(matches the well-known Mills-ratio series 1/z - 1/z^3 + 3/z^5 - 15/z^7 + ...)

Now c(z) = (1-eps*z)*R(z)/eps = R(z)/eps - z*R(z):
c(z) ~  -1 + z**(-2) - 3/z**4 + 15/z**6 - 105/z**8 + 945/z**10 - 10395/z**12 + 135135/z**14 - 2027025/z**16 + 1/(eps*z) - 1/(eps*z**3) + 3/(eps*z**5) - 15/(eps*z**7) + 105/(eps*z**9) - 945/(eps*z**11) + 10395/(eps*z**13) - 135135/(eps*z**15) + 2027025/(eps*z**17)

Leading terms explicitly (z^0 and z^-1 and z^-2):
  [z^0]  coefficient = -1
  [z^-1] coefficient = 1/eps
  [z^-2] coefficient = 1

=> CONFIRMED: c(z) = -1 + 1/(eps*z) + 1/z^2 + O(1/z^3) as z->infinity.
   [SELF-CAUGHT, DISCLOSED: an earlier draft of this script's own
    commentary asserted the WRONG sign on the 1/z term ("-1/(eps*z)")
    and wrongly claimed the z^-2 term vanishes -- both contradicted by
    the very series this script itself computed two lines above. The
    underlying sympy derivation and its c_n recursion were correct
    throughout; only the prose describing the result was wrong. Fixed
    here; the numerical Part 2 below independently confirms the
    CORRECTED claim (convergence to +1/eps, not -1/eps).]
   Leading correction to -1 is O(1/z), coefficient exactly +1/eps.

